{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","prediction_set_name":"k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","paper_id":"2512.01839","judge_input_sha256":"718ebd2a4db8bf6a4f2dba27ac42208f76396c3efa2a37817d83ae54bfca0537","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2512.01839:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2512.01839:I001:U001","2512.01839:I001:U002","2512.01839:I001:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U002"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is that an L-infinity convection field lacks the trace regularity needed to define the DG face fluxes and jumps. ISSUE-004 instead concerns a missing error contribution in a local face-efficiency estimate for the discrete velocity jump; it does not diagnose ill-defined fluxes for admitted beta.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2512.01839:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2512.01839:I002:U001","2512.01839:I002:U002","2512.01839:I002:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U003"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is failure to state the sufficiently-large-penalty threshold required for coercivity. ISSUE-003 identifies a mismatch between two penalty coefficients in primal and adjoint bilinear forms, which is a formulation-equivalence error and does not establish the coercivity threshold condition.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2512.01839:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2512.01839:I004:U001","2512.01839:I004:U002","2512.01839:I004:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U003"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"Both address regularity-dependent spectral arguments, but the gold defect is the unassumed adjoint source regularity needed to prove the analogue of s2.76 and the operator chain. ISSUE-002 diagnoses an interpolation-weight and convergence-rate mismatch in s2.88, not the missing adjoint regularity hypothesis.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2512.01839:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2512.01839:I005:U001","2512.01839:I005:U002","2512.01839:I005:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is that individual eigenvectors in a multiple semisimple eigenspace require compatible alignment, whereas ISSUE-001 concerns invalid H(div) projection estimates for a full tensor-jump DG norm. Its mention of spectral consequences does not diagnose eigenspace-basis alignment.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2512.01839:I008","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2512.01839:I008:U001","2512.01839:I008:U002","2512.01839:I008:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U003","ISSUE-004:U005"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is an invalid l1-to-global-l2 residual aggregation that loses mesh independence in the reliability proof. ISSUE-004 concerns a different local face-efficiency formula missing the discrete-velocity/L2 error contribution; it does not diagnose residual-sum aggregation.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}